  "provider_query": "PEP 703 page that proposes making the CPython GIL optional",
  "answer": "**PEP 703** proposes an optional no-GIL CPython build so multiple threads can run Python code in parallel.\n\n### Primary page\n1. **[PEP 703 – Making the Global Interpreter Lock Optional in CPython](https://peps.python.org/pep-0703/)** — Official PEP. Author Sam Gross; sponsor Łukasz Langa; created 9 Jan 2023; type Standards Track; targets Python 3.13. Status is now **Final** (historical). It adds a `--disable-gil` configure flag, defines `Py_GIL_DISABLED`, and uses an ABI tag with **“t”** (free-threaded). The GIL stays the default. Canonical follow-on docs: [Python support for free threading](https://docs.python.org/3/howto/free-threading-python.html). [web:8]\n\n### Related sources\n2. **[Steering Council acceptance (24 Oct 2023)](https://discuss.python.org/t/pep-703-making-the-global-interpreter-lock-optional-in-cpython-acceptance/37075)** — Accepts PEP 703 with a gradual rollout: experimental, then supported but not default, then possibly default; rollback allowed. Suggests the term **free-threaded**. [web:3]\n\n3. **[Steering Council intent notice (28 Jul 2023)](https://discuss.python.org/t/a-steering-council-notice-about-pep-703-making-the-global-interpreter-lock-optional-in-cpython/30474)** — Earlier intent to accept; outlines the three phases and a long-term preference for a single no-GIL build. [web:7]\n\n4. **[PEP 779 – Criteria for supported status for free-threaded Python](https://peps.python.org/pep-0779/)** — Phase II criteria (officially supported, still not default). Points to Python 3.14 for that step; Phase III (default) left for a later decision. [web:9]\n\n5. **[What is PEP 703? (pydevtools handbook)](https://pydevtools.com/handbook/explanation/what-is-pep-703.md)** — Short explainer: experimental in 3.13, officially supported in 3.14 under PEP 779; separate ABI (`t`); default builds still have the GIL. [web:1]\n\n6. **[Original PEP PR #2955](https://github.com/python/peps/pull/2955)** — GitHub PR that added the PEP (merged 10 Jan 2023). [web:4]\n\n7. **[Initial Discourse thread](https://discuss.python.org/t/pep-703-making-the-global-interpreter-lock-optional/22606)** — Early discussion of the proposal (including configure-flag naming). [web:5]\n\n8. **[PEP 803 – “abi3t”: Stable ABI for free-threaded builds](https://peps.python.org/pep-0803/)** — Follow-on packaging/ABI work that depends on PEP 703. [web:11]",
